From: RagnarokMac <noreply@ragnarokmac>
Subject: [PATCH] Renderer: do not register the same callback twice

Renderer.render(fn) pushed onto renderCallbacks unconditionally. Components
call it every time they are shown or switch tabs -- Equipment does so from
three separate sites -- so a window opened N times runs its render callback
N times per frame.

Each of those runs does clearRect() and then an async sprite draw against the
globally bound 2D context, so concurrent copies interleave: one clears the
canvas while another is mid-draw. The visible result is flickering, ghosted
sprites (a character rendered with two heads) and item sprites landing on the
wrong canvas.

Registration is now idempotent, which is what every call site already assumes.
Renderer.stop(fn) still removes it.

--- a/src/Renderer/Renderer.js
+++ b/src/Renderer/Renderer.js
@@
 	static render(fn) {
-		if (fn) {
+		// Idempotent: callers register on every show/tab-change and never
+		// expect to be run more than once per frame.
+		if (fn && this.renderCallbacks.indexOf(fn) === -1) {
 			this.renderCallbacks.push(fn);
 		}
 
